{"output":"I’ll inspect the search flow and tests, add a guard against stale requests, and run the existing tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nThe controller applied every request’s completion, even after a newer search or a clear. I added a per-search ID and guarded each completion update. The existing tests cover normal behavior; I’ll also run an in-memory probe for stale successes, failures, and clearing.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts with per-search IDs. Only the latest request can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race probe; git diff --check.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts with per-search IDs. Only the latest request can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race probe; git diff --check.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":5,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short; find .. -name AGENTS.md -print","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-fair-2tip6hsn/search-4-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":380,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-969ea6e7e23cc4a7abddd27c5770adf4.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test && node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst oldItems = [{ id: 'old', title: 'Old', url: '/old' }];\nconst newItems = [{ id: 'new', title: 'New', url: '/new' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const timing of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('same');\n    const current = c.search('same');\n    if (timing === 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(newItems); await current; }\n    if (timing === 'cleared') await c.search('  ');\n    const expected = c.getState();\n    let notifications = 0;\n    const unsubscribe = c.subscribe(() => notifications++);\n    requests[0][outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? oldItems : new Error('stale'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), expected);\n    assert.equal(notifications, 1);\n    unsubscribe();\n    if (timing !== 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(newItems); await current; }\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), timing === 'cleared'\n      ? { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null }\n      : { query: 'same', results: newItems, loading: false, error: null });\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Race probe passed: stale success/failure while pending, after completion, and after clearing.');\nNODE\n git diff --check && git diff -- src/search/controller.ts; git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-fair-2tip6hsn/search-4-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":387,"stdout_bytes":2241,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-6dd826cfbc9a4a816cd35fe8355a7b51.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":37096,"output_tokens":1011},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":9728,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":9}}
